{"id": "P08327", "name": "Kim Nam-jung", "name_chinese": "Kim Nam-Jung", "country": "South Korea", "net_worth_usd_m": "965.2", "net_worth_source": "Forbes real-time (former)", "source_of_wealth": "Food", "industry": "food-beverage", "sec_insider_companies": "", "shared_with": "", "appears_on": "Forbes real-time (former) (2025); Forbes annual (2016-2022); Hurun Global (2017)", "focus": [], "forbes_profile_url": "https://www.forbes.com/profile/kim-nam-jung/", "wikidata_url": "", "forbes_bio": ["Kim Nam-jung is the chairman of Dongwon Industries, a conglomerate best known for its famous canned tunas in Korea.", "He is the younger son of Dongwon founder Kim Jae-chul, who started the business in 1969; his first overseas base was in Ghana in 1973.", "In addition to a wide range of packaged seafood, Dongwon provides outsourced meals, operates cold-storage facilities and has a logistics operation.", "He took over the position in 2019 when the elder Kim stepped down as Dongwon's chairman after 50 years."], "forbes_facts": ["Nam-jung joined the business in a blue-collar position in 1996.", "Dongwon acquired leading U.S. tuna brand StarKist in 2008."]}
